# xdp-sentinel protected destinations (default-deny; services mirrored from ufw)
#
# Format:  <ipv4> [iface]
#   <ipv4>  destination to put in default-deny. Only the ports ufw has open
#           (ALLOW/LIMIT, inbound, IPv4) reach it; everything else is dropped
#           before the rate limiter.
#   [iface] interface to apply it on. Omit to apply to every interface the
#           agent manages. For a host reached from the WAN side, name the WAN
#           ingress (e.g. vlan10) so LAN-side traffic is unaffected.
#
# Install as /etc/xdp-sentinel/protect.conf, then enable:
#   systemctl enable --now xdp-sentinel-ufw-sync.path xdp-sentinel-ufw-sync.service
#
# WARNING: default-deny is stateless/direction-agnostic. Protecting the box's
# own IP can drop replies to the box's own OUTBOUND connections (DNS, updates)
# that arrive on ephemeral ports. Safe for serve-only backends; for the box
# itself, validate first (see docs) or wait for the stateful management-plane
# exemption.

# Protect the box's management IP on the WAN ingress only:
# 192.168.1.193 vlan10

# Protect a serve-only backend on every managed interface:
# 192.168.1.173
